WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.612
Last, retiring AD CS, which
is the program's sixth wave.

2
00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:09.902
It applies only to the CAs and role services
that no longer serve a retained class;

3
00:00:09.902 --> 00:00:14.244
domain controller, LDAPS and RADIUS
certificates usually keep at

4
00:00:14.244 --> 00:00:18.587
least one issuing CA alive for as
long as domain controllers exist.

5
00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:23.784
The gate: cutover complete, the thirty-day
rollback window passed with no incidents,

6
00:00:23.784 --> 00:00:27.249
and every retained class
running on the CAs that remain.

7
00:00:27.249 --> 00:00:29.565
Confirm nothing depends on the CA,

8
00:00:29.565 --> 00:00:33.037
using the lifecycle inventory
and the CA database.

9
00:00:33.037 --> 00:00:35.909
Stop new issuance: remove the templates,

10
00:00:35.909 --> 00:00:39.301
unlink autoenrollment,
deny pending requests.

11
00:00:39.301 --> 00:00:40.915
Back up the database and key,

12
00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:44.425
with the backup and its password
through separate channels.

13
00:00:44.425 --> 00:00:48.257
Revoke outstanding certificates
for cessation of operation,

14
00:00:48.257 --> 00:00:52.900
set the CRL lifetime past the remaining
certificates' lifetime, and publish.

15
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.816
Remove NDES and the web
services before the CA,

16
00:00:56.816 --> 00:01:00.525
and move any OCSP
consumers to CRL checking.

17
00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:07.025
Clean up trust in Entra, Intune, Group
Policy, NTAuth and the lifecycle platform.

18
00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:12.648
Keep the CDP and AIA endpoints serving
until the last certificate expires, delete

19
00:01:12.648 --> 00:01:16.122
templates only after every
CA in the forest is gone,

20
00:01:16.122 --> 00:01:18.437
and commit a decommission record.

21
00:01:18.437 --> 00:01:24.651
Under BYOCA, the root and any CA that
signed the Cloud PKI issuing CA stay.

22
00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:30.378
The assessor reads NIST
SP 800-53 evidence:

23
00:01:30.378 --> 00:01:34.421
key storage and binding settings
for IA-5 enhancement two,

24
00:01:34.421 --> 00:01:39.896
the trust store and CRL configuration
for path validation, HSM key protection

25
00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:44.950
for SC-12, and the certificate policy
and approved trust anchors for SC-17.

26
00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:50.464
So, from Monday: harden first and gate
on it, choose the root deliberately,

27
00:01:50.464 --> 00:01:55.978
issue strongly mapped certificates,
run both PKIs with reachable CRLs,

28
00:01:55.978 --> 00:01:58.688
and retire AD CS last, with evidence.

29
00:01:58.688 --> 00:02:03.438
Chapters 03 through 08 and the
appendices carry the detail.

30
00:02:03.438 --> 00:02:04.250
Thank you.
